# Two water channels crossing the deck, for M27 phase 2. The fixture for how
# water FLOWS, so both shapes the flow field can produce are here in one file.
#
# ROWS 5-6: ONE OUTLET. The water starts at column 4 with deck to its left, and
# runs to the right rail where the parapet is suppressed and it falls off. Only
# the right end touches somewhere the deck stops, so the whole channel flows one
# way and gets faster the nearer the fall.
#
# ROWS 10-11: TWO OUTLETS. The water spans the full width and both rails are
# open, so there is an outlet at each end and a WATERSHED down the middle. Cells
# flow to whichever rail is nearer, and the divide is calm because the speed
# tapers to zero there -- which is what stops two adjacent cells shoving in
# opposite directions at full strength and jittering a body straddling them.
#
# THE PARAPETS ARE SUPPRESSED ONLY WHERE THE WATER LEAVES. Everywhere else the
# derived railing stands, so the only way off the side of this segment is being
# carried off by the current -- which is the thing being tested, rather than an
# edge a player can wander over anywhere.
#
# ROWS 13-14: NO OUTLET AT ALL. A pond enclosed by deck on every side, so the
# flood has no sources and the field is empty there. It is in this file rather
# than borrowed from playtest_bridge because that map's pond has just become a
# channel -- and a claim about absence has to be made on ground built to have
# nothing, not on ground that happens not to have it yet.
#
# NOTHING ELSE IS IN HERE. Measuring a push on a fixture with rushers in it is
# how this project has repeatedly measured a rusher instead.

name = test_channel
base_height = 0
width = 21
length = 16
tags = foot, test

